DATE: 12 March 2025
COUNTRY: Nigeria
NUMBER OF DEATHS: 1
CAUSE: Struck by
ACTIVITY: Lifting, crane, rigging and deck operations
PRIMARY LIFE-SAVING RULE: Safe mechanical lifting
NARRATIVE
A rigger was guiding a pipe bundle onto a flatbed trailer during a lifting operation. The load was dropped when a sling slipped from the hook and the bundle struck the rigger, who was standing beside the trailer. He died at the scene.
WHAT WENT WRONG
The sling was not seated in the hook latch and the lift was not stopped when the load began to tilt. The rigger was positioned within the swing radius of the suspended load.
CORRECTIVE ACTIONS AND RECOMMENDATIONS
Retrain riggers on sling inspection. Define exclusion zones around suspended loads. Fit hooks with positive locking latches.
CAUSAL FACTORS
PEOPLE (ACTS)
- Worker positioned in the line of fire
- Sling not seated correctly in hook
- Lift not stopped when load tilted
PROCESS (CONDITIONS)
- Hook without positive locking latch
- No exclusion zone defined for the lift

