DATE: 03 May 2025
COUNTRY: Angola
NUMBER OF DEATHS: 1
CAUSE: Struck by
ACTIVITY: Lifting, crane, rigging and deck operations
PRIMARY LIFE-SAVING RULE: Safe mechanical lifting
NARRATIVE
During a crane lift of a container on the deck of a production platform, the container was dropped from a height of three metres after a shackle pin failed. The falling container struck a deck crew member standing below the load path.
WHAT WENT WRONG
The shackle pin had worn beyond its limit and had not been identified at inspection. The load path crossed an area where people were working.
CORRECTIVE ACTIONS AND RECOMMENDATIONS
Replace the shackle inspection regime with a tagged colour-code system. Separate crane load paths from walkways. Review lift planning on all platforms.
CAUSAL FACTORS
PEOPLE (ACTS)
- Worker positioned in the line of fire
PROCESS (CONDITIONS)
- Worn shackle pin not detected at inspection
- Load path crossed a work area
- Inadequate lift planning
- Inadequate inspection regime

