DATE: 19 January 2025
COUNTRY: Indonesia
NUMBER OF DEATHS: 2
CAUSE: Vehicle incident
ACTIVITY: Transport - land
PRIMARY LIFE-SAVING RULE: Driving
NARRATIVE
A light vehicle carrying two contractors left a gravel road at night and rolled into a drainage channel. Neither occupant was wearing a seat belt and both were thrown from the vehicle. The driver had been working for fourteen hours.
WHAT WENT WRONG
The driver was fatigued and drove above the site speed limit. The road had no edge markers or barrier at the drainage channel.
CORRECTIVE ACTIONS AND RECOMMENDATIONS
Enforce seat belt use with in-vehicle monitoring. Limit driving hours. Install barriers and edge markers at roadside hazards.
CAUSAL FACTORS
PEOPLE (ACTS)
- Seat belts not worn
- Driving above the speed limit
- Driver continued while fatigued
PROCESS (CONDITIONS)
- Excessive working hours
- No barrier at drainage channel
- Poor road edge marking

DATE: 22 June 2025
COUNTRY: Malaysia
NUMBER OF DEATHS: 1
CAUSE: Fall from height
ACTIVITY: Construction, commissioning, decommissioning
PRIMARY LIFE-SAVING RULE: Working at height
NARRATIVE
A scaffolder fell from the third level of a scaffold while dismantling a platform at a gas processing plant. The worker was not connected to a fall arrest system and fell six metres onto the concrete below.
WHAT WENT WRONG
The scaffolder removed a guardrail to pass a board and did not reinstall it. No anchor point was provided at the working level.
CORRECTIVE ACTIONS AND RECOMMENDATIONS
Provide fixed anchor points for scaffold dismantling. Require supervisor check before guardrails are removed.
CAUSAL FACTORS
PEOPLE (ACTS)
- Fall arrest harness not connected
- Guardrail removed and not replaced
PROCESS (CONDITIONS)
- No anchor point at working level
- Inadequate supervision
- Dismantling method not planned

