DATE: 07 February 2025
COUNTRY: Norway
NUMBER OF DEATHS: 2
CAUSE: Explosions or burns
ACTIVITY: Maintenance, inspection, testing
PRIMARY LIFE-SAVING RULE: Hot work
NARRATIVE
Two welders were cutting a pipe support near a drain line on a platform when a fire started. Hydrocarbon vapour from the drain ignited and the flame burned both welders. Both died from burn injuries.
WHAT WENT WRONG
The hot work permit did not identify the drain line as a source of vapour. The drain had not been isolated or flushed before the cutting started.
CORRECTIVE ACTIONS AND RECOMMENDATIONS
Isolate and flush drains before hot work. Review all hot work permits for vapour sources. Install fixed gas detection in hot work areas.
CAUSAL FACTORS
PEOPLE (ACTS)
- Cutting started before drain was flushed
PROCESS (CONDITIONS)
- Permit did not list vapour source
- Drain not isolated
- No gas detection in work area
- Inadequate risk assessment

